---
title: "interest_rate_model - Trilinear Interest Rate Model (Scallop Lend)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_calc_utilization: utilization = total_borrows / total_supply
    q_calc_utilization --> q_check_phase1: check utilization thresholds
    q_check_phase1 --> q_phase1: utilization <= kink1
    q_phase1 --> q_calc_rate1: borrow_rate = base_rate + utilization * slope1
    q_calc_rate1 --> q_calc_supply_rate: phase 1 (low utilization)
    q_check_phase1 --> q_check_phase2: utilization > kink1
    q_check_phase2 --> q_phase2: utilization <= kink2
    q_phase2 --> q_calc_rate2: borrow_rate = rate_at_kink1 + (utilization - kink1) * slope2
    q_calc_rate2 --> q_calc_supply_rate: phase 2 (medium utilization)
    q_check_phase2 --> q_phase3: utilization > kink2
    q_phase3 --> q_calc_rate3: borrow_rate = rate_at_kink2 + (utilization - kink2) * slope3
    q_calc_rate3 --> q_calc_supply_rate: phase 3 (high utilization, steep increase)
    q_calc_supply_rate --> q_apply_fee: supply_rate = borrow_rate * utilization * (1 - reserve_factor)
    q_apply_fee --> [*]: return (borrow_rate, supply_rate)

    note right of q_check_phase1
        INV-001: trilinear model has 3 phases with increasing slopes
        INV-002: slope3 >> slope2 >> slope1 (steep increase at high utilization)
        INV-003: utilization = total_borrows / total_supply, 0 <= utilization <= 1
    end note

    note right of q_calc_supply_rate
        INV-004: supply_rate = borrow_rate * utilization * (1 - reserve_factor)
        INV-005: reserve_factor portion of interest goes to protocol
        INV-006: interest rates are per-pool configurable parameters
    end note
